{
  "dom_id": "step-75681",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Finding the Reciprocal of a Mixed Number",
  "problem": "Calculate the reciprocal of $-2\\,\\dfrac{1}{3}.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we write the mixed number as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n-2\\,\\dfrac{1}{3}=-\\dfrac{2\\cdot 3+1}{3}=-\\dfrac{7}{3}\n$$\n\nThen, we flip the numerator and the denominator, keeping the negative sign. Therefore, the reciprocal of $-2\\,\\dfrac{1}{3}$ is $-\\dfrac{3}{7}.$",
